ese changes people are willing to pay  a little bit more that that social  responsibility has become part of all  these business plans right many people  are with many companies you have to do  this stuff because of you know it's it's  the right thing to do III really think  and the return is there people are gonna  feel good about it over time people are  going to understand and when people say  to me the most important point I want to  make is when people say to me and I  can't afford a Nissan Leaf like you have  today I can't afford you know solar  panels like you have a six kilowatt  system and I say neither could I when I  started when I started in 1970 it was  very expensive to buy solar panels so I  didn't do that took me 20 years to buy  solar electric two decades but I did the  cheap and easy stuff and I save money  the electric car I bought 1970 was not  expensive like a Nissan Leaf or a Tesla  I couldn't afford a Tesla today I could  afford a leaf but this is pretty cool  though it's a very foolhardy cause I get  another series or something I'm buying  one but people who say they can't do it  the way I do it  agreed I couldn't either when I started  you don't run up Mount Everest you get  the base camp you get acclimated and  adjust and you see how high you can  climb some people aren't going to make  it to the summit some  people are never gonna be able to afford  solar electric but can you buy some  light bulbs to lower your energy bill  put money in your pocket right away  mm-hmm you know energy-saving thermostat  weather stripping bike riding when  weather and fitness permit public  transportation in defense avail  available near you home gardening home  composting all that stuff is dirt cheap  do that stuff and you're gonna see money  back right away I like the finish on  that segment what are you guys doing to  save some money and do something good  for the environment let us know in the  comments right down below

